Z||000000||Cooter||01-23-2001||09:32 PM||||I was able to sell the monster sized turbo that I had for a little more than I thougt that I could get for it, so maybe a little extra cash the wife doesn't know about could find it's way into a turbo for the 3.4<BR>What "size" would be a good compromise for this engine? I have been told a t-3 60 trim, but I have no idea if this is right. Maybe a turbo from a single 300Zx or a 280zx? There are lots of turbochargers for sale, but which one. . . ||||reg||1
Z||000001||gixxer||01-23-2001||10:28 PM||||Try this site <A HREF="http://www.turbofast.com.au/TFmatch.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.turbofast.com.au/TFmatch.html</A> <BR>it's fun and gives you an idea of what you need.<BR>Buy the book " Maximum Boost" by Corky Bell<BR>if you're planning on fabbing up some of your own plumbing.<BR>Or buy a kit.<BR>In any event, get the book.<BR>Have fun.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||01-24-2001||09:24 AM||||WOW! Great web site! Based on the "Turbo Match" calculator, a 2.8 using a T3 turbo with a 69 compressor trim, eight pounds of boost, without an intercooler, makes 219 bhp @ 5600 rpm. A 3.4 will make 265 bhp. Add an intercooler and the 3.4 will make 290 bhp or 311bhp with 10 puunds of boost. Thems big V8 numbers!<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000003||rogergarrison||01-24-2001||05:53 PM||||im with sillouwett on this one, I dont think you should install a turbo unless it comes as a complete setup, all parts designed to work with each other. I have a turbo on my 3.1 with some other mods and it dynoed on engine dyno around 270.||||reg||1
